do $$ declare m_KG_108_3 uuid; a_id uuid; q_id uuid; begin
  if not exists (select 1 from public.courses where id = 'KG-108') then return; end if;
  insert into public.modules (course_id, number, title, title_rw, intro, intro_rw, sort_order)
  values ('KG-108', 3, 'Communication, Conflict and Public Interaction', 'Itumanaho, Amakimbirane n''Ihuriro n''Abaturage', 'This module covers radio and reporting discipline, de-escalation, dealing with difficult behaviour, customer service alongside security, and working with colleagues and site staff.', 'Iki gice kigaruka ku murava kuri radio no mu gutanga raporo, kugabanya ubushyuhe, gucyuha imyitwarire igoye, serivisi ku bakiriya hamwe n''umutekano, no gukorana n''abo mukorana n''abakozi b''ahantu.', 3)
  returning id into m_KG_108_3;
  insert into public.lessons (module_id, number, title, title_rw, kind, body, body_rw, duration_minutes, sort_order)
  values (m_KG_108_3, '3.1', 'Radio and Reporting Discipline', 'Umurava kuri Radio no mu Gutanga Raporo', 'text', 'A radio channel is a shared resource that must remain immediately available, which means it is never used for conversation, complaint or anything that could wait. Transmissions follow a fixed structure: call sign, wait for acknowledgement, then a short message giving location, observation and requirement. Keep it factual and brief, since a long transmission is frequently garbled under pressure and rarely repeated accurately.

The difference between a basic and an advanced officer shows most clearly here. A transmission stating that something looks wrong tells a supervisor nothing they can act on. A transmission naming a location, describing a specific behaviour and stating what is requested — ''north loading bay, male in contractor uniform trying vehicle doors, requesting supervisor'' — allows an immediate decision. Test the radio at the start of every shift and know where coverage fails, because discovering a dead zone during an incident is a discovery made at the worst possible moment.', 'Umurongo wa radio ni umutungo usangiwe ugomba kuguma ushobora gukoreshwa ako kanya, bivuze ko utigera ukoreshwa mu kiganiro, ikirego cyangwa ikintu cyose cyashobora gutegereza. Ubutumwa bukurikiza imiterere idahinduka: izina rya radio, gutegereza kwemererwa, hanyuma ubutumwa bugufi butanga ahantu, icyabonetse n''icyo usaba. Bugumishe bushingiye ku byabaye kandi bugufi, kuko ubutumwa burebure akenshi butasobanuka mu gitutu.

Itandukaniro riri hagati y''umukozi w''ibanze n''uwisumbuye rigaragarira neza hano. Ubutumwa buvuga ko hari ikintu kitameze neza nta cyo bubwira umugenzuzi ashobora gukoraho. Ubutumwa buvuga ahantu, busobanura imyitwarire yihariye kandi buvuga icyo usaba — ''aho ibicuruzwa bimanukira mu majyaruguru, umugabo wambaye umwenda w''ukora ku masezerano agerageza imiryango y''imodoka, ndasaba umugenzuzi'' — butuma hafatwa icyemezo ako kanya. Suzuma radio mu ntangiriro ya buri kazi umenye aho itagera.', 12, 1);
  insert into public.lessons (module_id, number, title, title_rw, kind, body, body_rw, duration_minutes, sort_order)
  values (m_KG_108_3, '3.2', 'De-escalation Techniques', 'Ubuhanga bwo Kugabanya Ubushyuhe', 'text', 'De-escalation is the most valuable practical skill an officer can hold, because a situation resolved through conversation costs nothing while every physical option costs something and carries risk. The sequence is four steps. Listen fully without interrupting, since interruption is itself an escalation and a person who has not finished speaking cannot begin listening. Acknowledge the person''s frustration explicitly, which concedes nothing but reliably lowers the temperature. Act within your authority to resolve whatever can be resolved. Refer anything beyond it promptly, telling the person exactly what will happen next.

Supporting behaviours matter as much as the words. Keep a respectful physical distance and adjust it to the person''s response. Keep your hands visible and your posture open rather than squared. Speak at a lower volume than they do, since matching volume escalates and dropping below it frequently draws them down. Move the interaction away from an audience where possible, because an audience makes it much harder for the other person to back down without losing face.', 'Kugabanya ubushyuhe ni bwo bumenyi bufatika bufite agaciro kanini umukozi ashobora kugira, kuko imimerere ikemuwe n''ikiganiro nta cyo itwara mu gihe buri buryo bw''umubiri butwara ikintu kandi bufite ibyago. Urutonde ni intambwe enye. Umva byose udahagarika ijambo, kuko guhagarika ijambo ubwabyo ari ukongera ubushyuhe kandi umuntu utararangiza kuvuga adashobora gutangira kumva. Emera uburakari bw''uwo muntu mu magambo agaragara, bitatanga ikintu ariko bigabanya ubushyuhe buri gihe. Kora mu bubasha bwawe ukemure ibishobora gukemuka. Ohereza ikirengeje vuba, ubwira uwo muntu neza icyo kizakurikiraho.

Imyitwarire ishyigikira ifite akamaro nk''ak''amagambo. Gumana intera y''icyubahiro y''umubiri kandi uyihindure ukurikije uko asubiza. Gumisha amaboko yawe agaragara n''imyifatire ifunguye aho kwerekana ko ushaka guhangana. Vuga ku ijwi riri hasi kurusha irye, kuko guhuza ijwi byongera ubushyuhe naho kurimanura akenshi bimumanura na we. Kura ikiganiro aho abantu bareba bishoboka.', 12, 2);
  insert into public.lessons (module_id, number, title, title_rw, kind, body, body_rw, duration_minutes, sort_order)
  values (m_KG_108_3, '3.3', 'Handling Difficult Behaviour', 'Gucyuha Imyitwarire Igoye', 'text', 'Difficult behaviour has causes, and identifying the cause frequently resolves the situation faster than responding to the behaviour. A person who is angry may be frustrated by something that has nothing to do with you; a person who is confused may be lost, unwell or affected by a medical condition frequently mistaken for intoxication; a person who is intoxicated has reduced capacity to process instruction and will need simpler, slower communication rather than firmer.

With an intoxicated or agitated person, the objective is a safe outcome rather than winning the exchange — get them to leave, to sit down or to wait, whichever is safest, and do not require them to acknowledge that you were right. Involve a colleague as a witness for any interaction likely to be disputed, and never place yourself alone in an enclosed space with a person behaving unpredictably. Where a person will not comply and the situation is deteriorating, withdraw and call for support rather than escalating, because an officer who is alone and committed has removed their own options.', 'Imyitwarire igoye ifite impamvu, kandi kumenya impamvu akenshi bikemura imimerere vuba kurusha gusubiza imyitwarire. Umuntu warakaye ashobora kuba yararakajwe n''ikintu kitagira aho gihuriye na wowe; umuntu ufite urujijo ashobora kuba yarazimiye, arwaye cyangwa afite ikibazo cy''ubuzima kikunze kwitiranywa no gusinda; umuntu wasinze afite ubushobozi buke bwo gutunganya itegeko kandi azakenera itumanaho ryoroshye, ritinda aho gukenera irikomeye.

Ku muntu wasinze cyangwa warakaye, intego ni icyavuyemo gifite umutekano aho kuba ugutsinda impaka — mutume agende, yicare cyangwa ategereze, icyo ari cyo cyose gifite umutekano, kandi ntumusabe kwemera ko wari ufite ukuri. Jyana mugenzi wawe nk''umuhamya ku ihuriro ryose rishobora kuvugwaho impaka, kandi ntukigere wishyira wenyine mu mwanya wugaranye n''umuntu witwara mu buryo butateganywa. Aho umuntu atazakurikiza kandi ibintu bikaza, subira inyuma uhamagare ubufasha aho kongera ubushyuhe.', 12, 3);
  insert into public.lessons (module_id, number, title, title_rw, kind, body, body_rw, duration_minutes, sort_order)
  values (m_KG_108_3, '3.4', 'Customer Service and Security Together', 'Serivisi ku Bakiriya n''Umutekano Hamwe', 'text', 'On most sites the officer is the first person a visitor speaks to, which makes service capability a job requirement rather than an optional strength. The two functions are not in tension as often as officers assume: a visitor who has been greeted, helped and treated with courtesy is far more likely to comply with a request, to answer a question honestly and to report something they noticed than one who has been processed.

Practically: greet first rather than waiting to be approached; give directions properly rather than pointing; explain the reason for a requirement where you can, since a person who understands why complies willingly while a person given a bare instruction complies resentfully or not at all; and never make a person feel suspected when they have done nothing. The exception is where service and security genuinely conflict — confirming whether a named person is present, allowing access to someone without authorisation, letting a delivery through unchecked — and in those cases security governs, politely and without apology.', 'Ku hantu henshi umukozi ni we muntu wa mbere umushyitsi avugana na we, bigatuma ubushobozi bwa serivisi ari ikisabwa mu murimo aho kuba imbaraga y''inyongera. Iyo mirimo ibiri ntabwo ihabanye kenshi nk''uko abakozi biyumvisha: umushyitsi wasuhujwe, wafashijwe kandi wafashwe mu cyubahiro ashoboka cyane kurushaho gukurikiza icyifuzo, gusubiza ikibazo mu kuri no gutanga ikintu yabonye kurusha uwatunganyijwe gusa.

Mu bikorwa: suhuza mbere aho gutegereza ko wegerwa; tanga inzira neza aho kuyereka n''urutoki; sobanura impamvu y''igisabwa aho ushobora, kuko umuntu usobanukiwe impamvu akurikiza ku bushake mu gihe umuntu wahawe itegeko gusa akurikiza arakaye cyangwa ntakurikize na gato; kandi ntukigere utuma umuntu yumva ko akekwaho nta cyo yakoze. Kirengagizwa ni aho serivisi n''umutekano bihabanye koko — kwemeza niba umuntu wavuzwe ahari, kwemerera kwinjira umuntu utemerewe, kwemerera ibicuruzwa kunyura bitagenzuwe — kandi muri ibyo umutekano ni wo ugenga, mu cyubahiro kandi utasabye imbabazi.', 12, 4);
  insert into public.lessons (module_id, number, title, title_rw, kind, body, body_rw, duration_minutes, sort_order)
  values (m_KG_108_3, '3.5', 'Working with Colleagues and Site Staff', 'Gukorana n''Abo Mukorana n''Abakozi b''Ahantu', 'text', 'Security depends on information held by people who are not security: reception sees an unusual visitor pattern, cleaning staff notice a door that has been propped, maintenance knows which lock has failed, and delivery staff see who is coming and going at the back. That information reaches the security team only where the relationship is cooperative rather than policing, and where a person who reports something sees that it was acted on.

Practical measures: introduce yourself to the staff on your site rather than remaining anonymous; ask them what they notice rather than waiting to be told; give visible feedback when their information leads to action, because a person whose report is never acknowledged concludes correctly that it was not used; and never treat site staff as suspects in front of others. Among colleagues, hand over properly at every shift change — anything unusual observed, any fault, any area currently unsecured, any person of interest — because knowledge held by one officer is lost entirely if it is not transferred.', 'Umutekano ushingira ku makuru ari ku bantu batari ab''umutekano: aho bakirirwa babona uburyo budasanzwe bw''abashyitsi, abasukura babona umuryango wafunguwe ukaba usigaye, abasana bazi ingufuli yapfuye, kandi abazana ibicuruzwa babona uwinjira n''uwasohotse inyuma. Ayo makuru agera ku itsinda ry''umutekano gusa aho umubano ari uw''ubufatanye aho kuba uwo gukurikirana, n''aho umuntu utanze ikintu abona ko cyakorewe.

Ingamba zifatika: imenyekanishe ku bakozi bo ku hantu hawe aho kuguma utazwi; babaze icyo babona aho gutegereza ko babikubwira; tanga ibitekerezo bigaragara igihe amakuru yabo yatumye habaho igikorwa, kuko umuntu raporo ye itigera yemerwa yemeza neza ko itakoreshejwe; kandi ntukigere ufata abakozi b''ahantu nk''abakekwaho imbere y''abandi. Mu bo mukorana, hererekanya neza kuri buri mpinduka y''akazi — ikintu cyose kidasanzwe cyabonetse, ikibazo cy''ibikoresho, agace katarinzwe, umuntu ushishikaje — kuko ubumenyi umukozi umwe afite butakara burundu nibudahererekanywa.', 12, 5);
