do $$ declare m_KG_108_4 uuid; a_id uuid; q_id uuid; begin
  if not exists (select 1 from public.courses where id = 'KG-108') then return; end if;
  insert into public.modules (course_id, number, title, title_rw, intro, intro_rw, sort_order)
  values ('KG-108', 4, 'Incident Response and Emergency Procedures', 'Gutabara Ibibazo n''Inzira z''Ibyihutirwa', 'This module covers responding to an incident, fire and evacuation, medical emergencies, theft and criminal incidents, and securing a scene.', 'Iki gice kigaruka ku gutabara ikibazo, inkongi no kwimuka, ibibazo bya muganga, ubujura n''ibyaha, no kurinda ahabaye ikibazo.', 4)
  returning id into m_KG_108_4;
  insert into public.lessons (module_id, number, title, title_rw, kind, body, body_rw, duration_minutes, sort_order)
  values (m_KG_108_4, '4.1', 'Responding to an Incident', 'Gutabara Ikibazo', 'text', 'The response sequence to any incident is the same regardless of type, and following it in order prevents most of the errors that occur under pressure. Assess before acting: what is happening, is it still happening, is the area safe to enter, and what will you be walking into. An officer who becomes a second casualty has removed the only responder present. Communicate early and specifically, giving location, nature and what is required, because a supervisor cannot send help to an address you have not stated. Act within your training and authority and no further. Record what you observed, when, and what you did.

The priority order never changes: protect life first, then contain the situation to prevent it spreading, then preserve evidence, then protect property. Officers under pressure frequently invert this and attempt to protect property or gather information before the situation is safe, which is how a manageable incident becomes an injury. Where the situation exceeds your authority or training, your job is to summon the people whose job it is rather than to attempt it yourself.', 'Urutonde rw''igisubizo ku kibazo icyo ari cyo cyose ni rumwe utitaye ku bwoko, kandi kurukurikiza mu rutonde bikumira amakosa menshi abaho mu gitutu. Suzuma mbere yo gukora: ni iki kiri kuba, ese kiracyabaho, ese agace gafite umutekano wo kwinjiramo, kandi ni iki ugiye kwinjiramo. Umukozi uhinduka uwakomeretse wa kabiri aba yakuyeho umutabazi wenyine uhari. Vugana kare kandi mu buryo bwihariye, utanga ahantu, ubwoko n''icyo gikenewe, kuko umugenzuzi adashobora kohereza ubufasha ku hantu utavuze. Kora mu mipaka y''amahugurwa n''ububasha bwawe kandi ntukarenge. Andika ibyo wabonye, ryari, n''ibyo wakoze.

Urutonde rw''ibyihutirwa ntiruhinduka: kurinda ubuzima mbere, hanyuma kugarura imimerere kugira ngo itakwira, hanyuma kubika ibimenyetso, hanyuma kurinda umutungo. Abakozi bari mu gitutu akenshi bahindura urutonde bakagerageza kurinda umutungo cyangwa gukusanya amakuru mbere y''uko ahantu hagira umutekano, ari bwo buryo ikibazo gishobora gucungwa gihinduka ikomere.', 12, 1);
  insert into public.lessons (module_id, number, title, title_rw, kind, body, body_rw, duration_minutes, sort_order)
  values (m_KG_108_4, '4.2', 'Fire and Evacuation', 'Inkongi no Kwimuka', 'text', 'In a fire the officer''s role is to raise the alarm, evacuate people and guide the fire service — not to fight the fire, except where a very small fire can be safely tackled with the correct extinguisher, you have been trained on it and you have a clear escape route behind you. Any doubt on any of those three points means evacuate instead.

Know your site''s evacuation plan before it is needed: every exit including the ones nobody uses, the assembly point, the refuge points for people who cannot use stairs, and which areas are hardest to clear. During an evacuation, direct people firmly and calmly by the nearest safe exit, never use lifts, check the areas you are responsible for including toilets and store rooms, and close doors behind you to slow the spread. At the assembly point, account for people and report anyone unaccounted for to the fire service immediately, since that information determines what they do first. Never re-enter a building, and never allow anyone else to, until the fire service declares it safe.', 'Mu nkongi umurimo w''umukozi ni ugutera induru, kwimura abantu no kuyobora abazimya — atari ukurwanya inkongi, uretse aho inkongi ntoya cyane ishobora kuzimywa mu mutekano ukoresheje icyuma cy''umuriro gikwiye, warabihuguriwe kandi ufite inzira isobanutse yo gusohoka inyuma yawe. Gushidikanya ku kimwe muri ibyo bitatu bivuze kwimuka ahubwo.

Menya gahunda yo kwimuka y''ahantu hawe mbere y''uko ikenerwa: buri rusohokerwa harimo n''izo nta muntu ukoresha, ahantu ho guhurira, ahantu h''uburinzi ku bantu badashobora gukoresha amazamu, n''utuce tugoye kwimurwamo kurusha utundi. Mu gihe cyo kwimuka, yobora abantu ukomeye kandi utuje unyuze mu rusohokerwa rwa hafi rufite umutekano, ntukoreshe itara, genzura utuce ushinzwe harimo n''ubwiherero n''ububiko, kandi ufunge imiryango inyuma yawe kugira ngo utinze ukwira. Ku hantu ho guhurira, barura abantu kandi utangeho raporo ku wese utabaruwe ku bazimya ako kanya.', 12, 2);
  insert into public.lessons (module_id, number, title, title_rw, kind, body, body_rw, duration_minutes, sort_order)
  values (m_KG_108_4, '4.3', 'Medical Emergencies', 'Ibibazo bya Muganga', 'text', 'A medical emergency is the incident an officer is most likely to face and the one most sites are least prepared for. The sequence is: ensure the scene is safe before approaching, since an officer who becomes a second casualty helps nobody; assess responsiveness and breathing; send a specific named person to call emergency services and another to meet and guide them to the location, rather than assuming either will happen; provide first aid within the limits of your training and no further; and stay with the casualty until qualified help arrives.

Clear onlookers, both for the casualty''s dignity and to keep the access route open for the ambulance. Do not move a casualty unless leaving them creates a greater danger. Record exact times throughout — when the incident occurred, when help was called, when it arrived — because the arriving medical team asks for those first. And hold a current first aid qualification from a recognised provider: this content establishes the sequence and the priorities, and the practical skills of CPR, bleeding control and airway management must be learned and assessed hands-on with a certified instructor, because they degrade within months without practice.', 'Ikibazo cya muganga ni cyo kibazo umukozi ashoboka kurusha ibindi guhura na cyo kandi ni cyo ahantu henshi hitegura bike kurusha ibindi. Urutonde ni: kwemeza ko ahantu hafite umutekano mbere yo kwegera, kuko umukozi uhinduka uwakomeretse wa kabiri nta muntu afasha; gusuzuma niba asubiza kandi ahumeka; kohereza umuntu umwe wagenwe guhamagara abatabazi n''undi kubakira no kubayobora aho hantu, aho kwiyumvisha ko bizabaho; gutanga ubufasha bwa mbere mu mipaka y''amahugurwa yawe kandi ntukarenge; no kuguma n''uwakomeretse kugeza ubufasha bufite ubumenyi bugeze.

Kura abareba, ku bw''icyubahiro cy''uwakomeretse no kugira ngo inzira igume ifunguye ku modoka y''abatabazi. Ntukimure uwakomeretse keretse kumusiga bitera akaga kanini kurushaho. Andika amasaha nyayo muri byose. Kandi ugire icyemezo kigezweho cy''ubufasha bwa mbere kiva ku kigo cyemewe: ibi bishyiraho urutonde n''ibyihutirwa, kandi ubumenyi bufatika bwa CPR, guhagarika amaraso no gucunga inzira y''umwuka bugomba kwigwa bukanasuzumwa ku bikoresho n''umwarimu wemewe.', 12, 3);
  insert into public.lessons (module_id, number, title, title_rw, kind, body, body_rw, duration_minutes, sort_order)
  values (m_KG_108_4, '4.4', 'Theft, Damage and Criminal Incidents', 'Ubujura, Kwangiza n''Ibyaha', 'text', 'When a criminal incident occurs, an officer''s role is to observe, record, report and preserve — not to investigate and not, in most circumstances, to detain. Detention carries substantial legal risk, follows the specific and narrow rules of the jurisdiction, and converts an incident into a legal proceeding in which the officer is personally exposed. The rules of engagement for your site should state clearly whether detention is permitted and on what basis, and where they do not, the answer is that it is not.

What is genuinely valuable is accurate observation. Record a description systematically — build, height, clothing from head down, distinguishing features, direction of travel, and a vehicle description with as much of the registration as you saw. Note the exact time. Do not touch anything at the scene. Do not discuss the incident with other witnesses before each has given their own account, since accounts merge through discussion and a merged account is worth considerably less. Report immediately rather than at the end of the shift, and write the report while recollection is accurate.', 'Igihe icyaha kibaye, umurimo w''umukozi ni ukwitegereza, kwandika, gutanga raporo no kubika — atari gukora iperereza kandi atari, mu bihe byinshi, gufunga umuntu. Gufunga bifite ibyago bikomeye by''amategeko, bikurikiza amategeko yihariye kandi magufi y''aho ukorera, kandi bihindura ikibazo urubanza aho umukozi agaragara ku giti cye. Amabwiriza y''ibikorwa y''ahantu hawe agomba kuvuga neza niba gufunga byemewe kandi hashingiwe kuki, kandi aho atabivuga, igisubizo ni uko bitemewe.

Icyingirakamaro koko ni ukwitegereza kunoze. Andika uko umuntu asa mu buryo buteguye — imiterere, uburebure, imyambaro uhereye hejuru, ibimuranga, icyerekezo agiye, n''imiterere y''imodoka n''igice cya nimero wabonye. Andika isaha nyayo. Ntugakore ku kintu ku hantu habaye ikibazo. Ntuganire ku kibazo n''abandi bahamya mbere y''uko buri wese atanga ibye, kuko ibivuzwe bivangwa mu kiganiro kandi ibyavanzwe bigira agaciro gake cyane. Tangaho raporo ako kanya aho kuyitanga ku iherezo ry''akazi.', 12, 4);
  insert into public.lessons (module_id, number, title, title_rw, kind, body, body_rw, duration_minutes, sort_order)
  values (m_KG_108_4, '4.5', 'Securing a Scene', 'Kurinda Ahabaye Ikibazo', 'text', 'Where an offence may have occurred or where an incident will be investigated, the officer''s task is to preserve the scene in the condition it was found, because evidence is fragile and most of it is destroyed by well-intentioned people in the first few minutes. Establish a boundary wider than the obvious area, since evidence extends beyond where the event visibly occurred — an approach route, a discarded item, a vehicle position.

Allow nobody to enter except those with a genuine operational reason, and record every person who does enter, when and why, because that record is what allows an investigator to distinguish evidence from contamination. Touch nothing, move nothing, clean nothing and do not allow anyone else to, including managers who want the area returned to use — a scene released before it has been examined cannot be recovered. Note the original position of anything that has to be moved for safety. Record what you observed on arrival and the exact time. And hand over to the investigating authority with a clear account of what was done, by whom and when.', 'Aho icyaha gishobora kuba cyarabaye cyangwa aho ikibazo kizakorwaho iperereza, umurimo w''umukozi ni ukubika ahantu mu mimerere hasanzwemo, kuko ibimenyetso ari bito kandi byinshi muri byo bisenywa n''abantu bafite intego nziza mu minota mike ya mbere. Shyiraho imbibi zagutse kurusha agace kagaragara, kuko ibimenyetso birenga aho ibintu byabereye bigaragara — inzira yanyuzwemo, ikintu cyajugunywe, aho imodoka yari ihagaze.

Ntukemerere umuntu kwinjira uretse abafite impamvu nyayo y''akazi, kandi wandike buri muntu winjira, ryari n''impamvu, kuko iyo nyandiko ari yo ituma umushakashatsi atandukanya ibimenyetso n''ibyanduye. Ntugakore ku kintu, ntukimure ikintu, ntusukure ikintu kandi ntukemerere undi kubikora, harimo n''abayobozi bashaka ko agace kagaruka gukoreshwa — ahantu harekuwe hatarasuzumwa ntihashobora kugarurwa. Andika aho ikintu cyari kiri mbere niba kigomba kwimurwa ku mpamvu z''umutekano. Andika ibyo wabonye ugeze n''isaha nyayo. Kandi uhererekanye ku rwego rukora iperereza.', 12, 5);
  insert into public.assessments (course_id, module_id, title, title_rw, kind, pass_mark, sort_order)
  values ('KG-108', m_KG_108_4, 'Quiz — Incident Response and Emergency Procedures', 'Ikizamini — Gutabara Ibibazo n''Inzira z''Ibyihutirwa', 'quiz', 70, 4)
  returning id into a_id;
  insert into public.questions (assessment_id, number, kind, prompt, prompt_rw, points, sort_order)
  values (a_id, 1, 'mcq', 'What is the priority order in any incident?', 'Ni uruhe rutonde rw''ibyihutirwa mu kibazo icyo ari cyo cyose?', 1, 1) returning id into q_id;
  insert into public.question_options (question_id, label, label_rw, is_correct, sort_order)
  values (q_id, 'Protect life, contain, preserve evidence, protect property', 'Kurinda ubuzima, kugarura, kubika ibimenyetso, kurinda umutungo', true, 1);
  insert into public.question_options (question_id, label, label_rw, is_correct, sort_order)
  values (q_id, 'Judgement — deciding correctly where no procedure anticipated the situation', 'Ubushishozi — gufata icyemezo cyiza aho nta nzira yateganyije', false, 2);
  insert into public.question_options (question_id, label, label_rw, is_correct, sort_order)
  values (q_id, 'No — they survive it permanently', 'Oya — zikomeza burundu', false, 3);
  insert into public.question_options (question_id, label, label_rw, is_correct, sort_order)
  values (q_id, 'A baseline of what is normal here, at this hour, with these people', 'Ishingiro ry''ibisanzwe hano, kuri iyi saha, n''aba bantu', false, 4);
  insert into public.questions (assessment_id, number, kind, prompt, prompt_rw, points, sort_order)
  values (a_id, 2, 'mcq', 'When may an officer tackle a fire?', 'Ni ryari umukozi ashobora kurwanya inkongi?', 1, 2) returning id into q_id;
  insert into public.question_options (question_id, label, label_rw, is_correct, sort_order)
  values (q_id, 'A master key defeats every other physical measure simultaneously', 'Urufunguzo rukuru rutsinda izindi ngamba zose icyarimwe', false, 1);
  insert into public.question_options (question_id, label, label_rw, is_correct, sort_order)
  values (q_id, 'A medical condition causing confusion', 'Ikibazo cy''ubuzima gitera urujijo', false, 2);
  insert into public.question_options (question_id, label, label_rw, is_correct, sort_order)
  values (q_id, 'Accounts merge through discussion and a merged account is worth much less', 'Ibivuzwe bivangwa mu kiganiro kandi ibyavanzwe bigira agaciro gake', false, 3);
  insert into public.question_options (question_id, label, label_rw, is_correct, sort_order)
  values (q_id, 'Only if it is very small, they are trained, the correct extinguisher is present and an escape route is clear', 'Gusa niba ari ntoya, yarahuguwe, icyuma gikwiye kihari n''inzira isobanutse', true, 4);
  insert into public.questions (assessment_id, number, kind, prompt, prompt_rw, points, sort_order)
  values (a_id, 3, 'mcq', 'Why should witnesses not discuss an incident before giving accounts?', 'Kuki abahamya batagomba kuganira ku kibazo mbere yo gutanga ibivuzwe?', 1, 3) returning id into q_id;
  insert into public.question_options (question_id, label, label_rw, is_correct, sort_order)
  values (q_id, 'A single unexplained gap in the continuity record', 'Icyuho kimwe kitasobanuwe mu nyandiko y''ugukomeza', false, 1);
  insert into public.question_options (question_id, label, label_rw, is_correct, sort_order)
  values (q_id, 'The only warning you will receive before the injury — report it as seriously', 'Bwo burira bwonyine uzabona mbere y''ikomere — butangeho raporo ku buremere bumwe', false, 2);
  insert into public.question_options (question_id, label, label_rw, is_correct, sort_order)
  values (q_id, 'Accounts merge through discussion and a merged account is worth much less', 'Ibivuzwe bivangwa mu kiganiro kandi ibyavanzwe bigira agaciro gake', true, 3);
  insert into public.question_options (question_id, label, label_rw, is_correct, sort_order)
  values (q_id, 'A scene released before it has been examined', 'Ahantu harekuwe hatarasuzumwa', false, 4);
  insert into public.questions (assessment_id, number, kind, prompt, prompt_rw, points, sort_order)
  values (a_id, 4, 'mcq', 'What cannot be recovered once done?', 'Ni iki kitagishobora kugarurwa kimaze gukorwa?', 1, 4) returning id into q_id;
  insert into public.question_options (question_id, label, label_rw, is_correct, sort_order)
  values (q_id, 'Enforced for the unfamiliar and waived for those who look like they belong', 'Rikurikizwa ku batazwi rigasibwa ku bagaragara nk''abo aho', false, 1);
  insert into public.question_options (question_id, label, label_rw, is_correct, sort_order)
  values (q_id, 'A scene released before it has been examined', 'Ahantu harekuwe hatarasuzumwa', true, 2);
  insert into public.question_options (question_id, label, label_rw, is_correct, sort_order)
  values (q_id, 'Only once the incoming officer has arrived, been briefed and confirmed understanding', 'Gusa uje amaze kugera, kumenyeshwa no kwemeza ko yumvise', false, 3);
  insert into public.question_options (question_id, label, label_rw, is_correct, sort_order)
  values (q_id, 'The site owner''s property rights, lawfully delegated — not the uniform', 'Uburenganzira bwa nyir''ahantu bwahawe — atari umwenda', false, 4);
end $$;
do $$ declare m_KG_108_5 uuid; a_id uuid; q_id uuid; begin
  if not exists (select 1 from public.courses where id = 'KG-108') then return; end if;
  insert into public.modules (course_id, number, title, title_rw, intro, intro_rw, sort_order)
  values ('KG-108', 5, 'Reporting, Records and Evidence', 'Gutanga Raporo, Inyandiko n''Ibimenyetso', 'This module covers writing reports that stand up to scrutiny, the occurrence log, statements and evidence, handling CCTV and personal data, and giving evidence.', 'Iki gice kigaruka ku kwandika raporo zihagarara mu igenzura, igitabo cy''ibibaye, ibivuzwe n''ibimenyetso, gucunga kamera n''amakuru bwite, no gutanga ubuhamya.', 5)
  returning id into m_KG_108_5;
  insert into public.lessons (module_id, number, title, title_rw, kind, body, body_rw, duration_minutes, sort_order)
  values (m_KG_108_5, '5.1', 'Writing Reports That Stand Up', 'Kwandika Raporo Zihagarara', 'text', 'A report may be read months later by an investigator, an insurer, a lawyer or a court, and it will be judged on whether it is specific, factual and internally consistent. Write it while recollection is accurate rather than at the end of a shift, because detail degrades within hours and the details that seem unimportant at the time are frequently the ones that matter later.

Cover: what happened, when with exact times, where precisely, who was involved and who was present, what you did and in what order, and who you notified and when. Record observed fact rather than conclusion — ''the male was unsteady on his feet and his speech was slurred'' is an observation, while ''the male was drunk'' is a conclusion an officer is not qualified to draw and which a lawyer will dismantle. Distinguish clearly between what you saw yourself, what someone told you and what you inferred, because a reader who discovers that a stated fact was an inference will doubt everything else in the document. Never guess, never fill a gap, and never alter a report afterwards — if a correction is needed, add a dated amendment.', 'Raporo ishobora gusomwa hashize amezi n''umushakashatsi, ubwishingizi, umunyamategeko cyangwa urukiko, kandi izacirwaho urubanza ku kuba ari iyihariye, ishingiye ku byabaye kandi ihuye imbere muri yo. Yandike mu gihe kwibuka gukiri kunoze aho kuyandika ku iherezo ry''akazi, kuko ibirambuye byangirika mu masaha make.

Bikubiyemo: ibyabaye, ryari n''amasaha nyayo, hehe neza, ni bande babigizemo uruhare n''abari bahari, ibyo wakoze n''urutonde, n''uwo wamenyesheje n''igihe. Andika ibyabonetse aho kwandika umwanzuro — ''uwo mugabo yagendaga adahagaze neza kandi imvugo ye ntiyumvikanaga'' ni ikintu cyabonetse, mu gihe ''uwo mugabo yari yasinze'' ni umwanzuro umukozi adafite ubushobozi bwo gufata kandi umunyamategeko azasenya. Tandukanya neza ibyo wiboneye, ibyo umuntu yakubwiye n''ibyo wiyumvishije, kuko umusomyi uzamenya ko ikintu cyavuzwe nk''ukuri cyari icyiyumvishijwe azashidikanya ku bindi byose. Ntukagere, ntuzuze icyuho, kandi ntuhindure raporo nyuma — niba gukosora bikenewe, ongeraho impinduka ifite itariki.', 12, 1);
  insert into public.lessons (module_id, number, title, title_rw, kind, body, body_rw, duration_minutes, sort_order)
  values (m_KG_108_5, '5.2', 'The Occurrence Log', 'Igitabo cy''Ibibaye', 'text', 'The occurrence log is the continuous record of a shift and it is the document most often treated as a formality and most often needed later. Enter events at the time rather than reconstructing them at the end, because a log written retrospectively is visibly a reconstruction and carries far less weight. Record start and end of shift, handover details, patrols conducted with times, anything unusual observed even where it came to nothing, alarm activations and outcomes, visitors outside the routine, faults and defects reported, and any instruction received and from whom.

Write entries in chronological order without gaps, sign each, and never leave blank space that could later be filled — where a correction is needed, strike through with a single line, initial and date it rather than obliterating the original. The log''s real value is that it makes patterns visible across shifts and across weeks: three officers each noticing the same vehicle on different nights see nothing individually, while a log holding all three entries shows something none of them could see alone.', 'Igitabo cy''ibibaye ni inyandiko ikomeza y''akazi kandi ni yo nyandiko ikunze gufatwa nk''iy''imigenzo gusa kandi ikunze gukenerwa nyuma. Andika ibintu ku gihe aho kubyubaka ku iherezo, kuko igitabo cyanditse nyuma kigaragara ko cyubatswe kandi kigira uburemere buke cyane. Andika intangiriro n''iherezo ry''akazi, amakuru yo guhererekanya, patrouille zakozwe n''amasaha, ikintu cyose kidasanzwe cyabonetse n''aho kitaba ikintu, induru zavuze n''ibyavuyemo, abashyitsi bo hanze y''ibisanzwe, ibyapfuye byatanzweho raporo, n''itegeko iryo ari ryo ryose ryakiriwe n''uwaritanze.

Andika ibintu mu rutonde rw''igihe nta byuho, sinya kuri buri kimwe, kandi ntusige umwanya utanditseho ushobora kuzuzwa nyuma — aho gukosora bikenewe, ca umurongo umwe, ushyireho utwo mu mazina n''itariki aho gusiba ibyanditse. Agaciro nyako k''igitabo ni uko gituma uburyo bugaragara mu bihe by''akazi no mu byumweru: abakozi batatu buri wese abona imodoka imwe ku majoro atandukanye nta cyo babona ku giti cyabo, mu gihe igitabo gifite ibyo bintu bitatu byose kigaragaza ikintu nta n''umwe muri bo yashoboraga kubona.', 12, 2);
  insert into public.lessons (module_id, number, title, title_rw, kind, body, body_rw, duration_minutes, sort_order)
  values (m_KG_108_5, '5.3', 'Statements and Evidence', 'Ibivuzwe n''Ibimenyetso', 'text', 'A statement is a formal account of what you personally observed, and its value rests entirely on it being your own recollection rather than a merged version. Write it as soon as possible and independently — do not discuss the incident with other witnesses first, because accounts converge through conversation without anyone intending it and a converged account is worth considerably less than three independent ones.

Write in the first person, in chronological order, with exact times and precise locations. State what you saw, heard and did, and state explicitly where you did not see something rather than filling the gap — ''I did not see how he entered'' is a stronger statement than a guess that turns out to be wrong. Where physical evidence is involved, do not handle it unless there is a genuine reason, and where you must, record what you did, when and why. Continuity of evidence — an unbroken record of who held an item from the moment it was found — is what makes it usable, and a single unexplained gap in that record is frequently enough to render it worthless.', 'Ibivuzwe ni inyandiko yemewe y''ibyo wiboneye ubwawe, kandi agaciro kabyo gashingiye burundu ku kuba ari ukwibuka kwawe bwite aho kuba verisiyo yavanzwe. Byandike vuba bishoboka kandi wigenga — ntuganire ku kibazo n''abandi bahamya mbere, kuko ibivuzwe bihurira mu kiganiro nta muntu ubigambiriye kandi ibihuriye bigira agaciro gake cyane kurusha ibitatu byigenga.

Andika mu buryo bwa mbere, mu rutonde rw''igihe, n''amasaha nyayo n''ahantu nyaho. Vuga ibyo wabonye, wumvise n''ibyo wakoze, kandi uvuge neza aho utabonye ikintu aho kuzuza icyuho — ''ntanabonye uko yinjiye'' ni ivuga rikomeye kurusha ugukeka kugaragara ko atari ko byari. Aho ibimenyetso by''umubiri bibigizemo uruhare, ntubikoreho keretse hari impamvu nyayo, kandi aho bigomba, andika ibyo wakoze, ryari n''impamvu. Gukomeza kw''ibimenyetso — inyandiko idacitse y''uwafashe ikintu uhereye igihe cyabonetse — ni cyo gituma bikoreshwa.', 12, 3);
  insert into public.lessons (module_id, number, title, title_rw, kind, body, body_rw, duration_minutes, sort_order)
  values (m_KG_108_5, '5.4', 'CCTV and Personal Data', 'Kamera n''Amakuru Bwite', 'text', 'CCTV footage, visitor logs, access records and incident reports all contain personal data about identified individuals, much of it concerning people who have done nothing wrong, and all of it falls under data protection obligations. Access footage only for a genuine operational reason and record why you accessed it. Never show footage to a person without authority, never copy it to a personal device, and never share an image on a phone or messaging application — this is one of the most common serious disciplinary failures in the sector and it is straightforwardly unlawful in most jurisdictions.

Release footage only through the authorised process and to a party entitled to receive it, recording what was released, to whom and on what basis. Retain records only for the defined period and ensure deletion at expiry, since indefinite retention is a compliance failure in its own right. And be aware that a person recorded may have a right to request access to footage of themselves — handle such a request through the correct process rather than refusing or complying informally.', 'Amashusho ya kamera, igitabo cy''abashyitsi, inyandiko z''abinjiye n''raporo z''ibibazo byose birimo amakuru bwite y''abantu bazwi, byinshi muri byo bireba abantu nta cyo bakoze, kandi byose biri mu nshingano zo kurengera amakuru. Injira mu mashusho gusa ku mpamvu nyayo y''akazi kandi wandike impamvu wayinjiyemo. Ntukigere wereka amashusho umuntu utabifitiye ububasha, ntukigere uyakoporora ku gikoresho cyawe bwite, kandi ntukigere usangira ifoto kuri telefoni cyangwa porogaramu y''ubutumwa — iri ni rimwe mu makosa akomeye y''ikinyabupfura akunze kubaho muri uru rwego kandi ntiryemewe n''amategeko mu bihugu byinshi.

Tanga amashusho gusa unyuze mu nzira yemewe kandi ku ruhande rufite uburenganzira bwo kuyakira, wandika ibyatanzwe, kuri nde n''ishingiro. Bika inyandiko gusa mu gihe cyagenwe kandi wemeze ko zisibwa kirangiye, kuko kubika nta gihe ntarengwa ari ikosa ubwaryo. Kandi umenye ko umuntu wafashwe ashobora kugira uburenganzira bwo gusaba kubona amashusho ye.', 12, 4);
  insert into public.lessons (module_id, number, title, title_rw, kind, body, body_rw, duration_minutes, sort_order)
  values (m_KG_108_5, '5.5', 'Giving Evidence', 'Gutanga Ubuhamya', 'text', 'An officer may be required to give evidence to an investigator, a disciplinary panel, an insurer or a court, sometimes long after the event, and their credibility will rest on the quality of the record they made at the time. Prepare by reviewing your original report and log rather than by rehearsing what you intend to say, because a witness who has rehearsed sounds rehearsed and a witness relying on a contemporaneous record sounds reliable.

When giving evidence: answer only the question asked and stop; say ''I do not recall'' where you do not, since a guess that is later contradicted damages everything else you have said; distinguish clearly between what you saw yourself and what you were told; do not speculate about motive, intent or what a person was thinking, because you cannot know it and it is not what you are there for; and remain calm and factual regardless of how the questioning is conducted, since a witness who becomes defensive or argumentative loses credibility independently of whether they are right. Dress and behave professionally throughout — you are representing the standard of the whole operation.', 'Umukozi ashobora gusabwa gutanga ubuhamya ku mushakashatsi, akanama k''ikinyabupfura, ubwishingizi cyangwa urukiko, rimwe na rimwe hashize igihe kirekire nyuma y''ibyabaye, kandi kwizerwa kwe kuzashingira ku bwiza bw''inyandiko yakoze ku gihe. Witegure usuzuma raporo yawe ya mbere n''igitabo aho kwitoza ibyo ugambiriye kuvuga, kuko umuhamya wiyitoje agaragara ko yiyitoje kandi umuhamya wiringira inyandiko yakozwe ku gihe agaragara ko yizewe.

Mu gutanga ubuhamya: subiza gusa ikibazo cyabajijwe uhagarare; vuga ''sinibuka'' aho utibuka, kuko ugukeka kuzavuguruzwa nyuma kwangiza ibindi byose wavuze; tandukanya neza ibyo wiboneye n''ibyo wabwiwe; ntugakeke ku mpamvu, icyifuzo cyangwa ibyo umuntu yatekerezaga, kuko udashobora kubimenya kandi atari byo uhari; kandi guma utuje kandi ushingiye ku byabaye uko kubaza kwakorwa kose, kuko umuhamya urwanaho cyangwa ujya mu mpaka atakaza kwizerwa atitaye ku kuba afite ukuri. Wambare kandi witware mu buryo bw''umwuga muri byose.', 12, 5);
  insert into public.assessments (course_id, module_id, title, title_rw, kind, pass_mark, sort_order)
  values ('KG-108', m_KG_108_5, 'Quiz — Reporting, Records and Evidence', 'Ikizamini — Gutanga Raporo, Inyandiko n''Ibimenyetso', 'quiz', 70, 5)
  returning id into a_id;
