-- ---------- EP-V1 · Executive Protection — Volume 1: EP Fundamentals ----------
do $$ declare m_EP_V1_1 uuid; a_id uuid; q_id uuid; begin
  if not exists (select 1 from public.courses where id = 'EP-V1') then return; end if;
  insert into public.modules (course_id, number, title, title_rw, intro, intro_rw, sort_order)
  values ('EP-V1', 1, 'Origins, Role and Language of the Profession', 'Inkomoko, Umurimo n''Ururimi rw''Uyu Mwuga', 'Subjects 1–4. This module establishes what executive protection is, where it came from, what an EP specialist is actually accountable for, and the vocabulary the profession uses precisely.', 'Ingingo 1–4. Iki gice gishyiraho icyo kurinda abakomeye ari cyo, aho byavuye, ibyo umunyamwuga wa EP abazwa koko, n''amagambo uyu mwuga ukoresha mu buryo busobanutse.', 1)
  returning id into m_EP_V1_1;
  insert into public.lessons (module_id, number, title, title_rw, kind, body, body_rw, duration_minutes, sort_order)
  values (m_EP_V1_1, '1', 'Introduction to Executive Protection', 'Intangiriro ku Kurinda Abakomeye', 'text', 'Executive protection is the discipline of keeping one identified person — the principal — safe as they move through an environment that cannot be controlled in advance. It is defined by that single constraint. A site can be hardened, locked, screened and restricted; a principal cannot, because the entire purpose of the role is that the principal continues to live, work, travel and appear publicly as normal. Protection is therefore achieved by shaping the environment around the principal rather than by restricting the principal, and by working ahead of them in time rather than reacting around them in space. The measure of a well-run detail is a day on which nothing happened and nobody noticed the work that made it so.

The role is widely misunderstood, including within the security industry. The popular conception emphasises physical presence, size and dramatic intervention. In practice, the overwhelming majority of protective value is generated before the principal arrives anywhere: in the threat assessment, in the advance, in the route analysis, in the decision to decline a venue that cannot be controlled, and in the discipline of varying a routine so that no pattern is available to observe. An officer who understands this allocates their effort correctly; one who does not spends it on the visible ten per cent.', 'Kurinda abakomeye ni umwuga wo kugumisha umuntu umwe wagenwe — uwo barinda — mu mutekano mu gihe agenda mu hantu hadashobora kugenzurwa mbere. Bisobanurwa n''iyo nzitizi imwe. Ahantu hashobora gukomezwa, gufungwa, kugenzurwa no kugarukirwa; uwo barinda ntashobora, kuko intego yose y''uyu murimo ari uko uwo barinda akomeza kubaho, gukora, kugenda no kugaragara ku mugaragaro nk''uko bisanzwe. Kurinda rero bigerwaho bahindura ahantu hakikije uwo barinda aho kumugarukira, no gukora mbere ye mu gihe aho gusubiza ibimukikije mu mwanya. Igipimo cy''itsinda ricungwa neza ni umunsi nta cyabaye kandi nta muntu wabonye umurimo watumye bimeze bityo.

Uyu murimo usobanurwa nabi cyane, harimo no mu rwego rw''umutekano ubwarwo. Icyo abantu batekereza cyibanda ku kugaragara ku mubiri, ubunini no kugira icyo ukora gikomeye. Mu bikorwa, agaciro kanini cyane ko kurinda gakorwa mbere y''uko uwo barinda ageza ahantu hose: mu isuzuma ry''iterabwoba, mu murimo ubanziriza, mu isesengura ry''inzira, mu cyemezo cyo kwanga ahantu hadashobora kugenzurwa, no mu murava wo guhindura ibisanzwe kugira ngo nta buryo bugaragara bwo kwitegereza buhari. Umukozi ubisobanukiwe agabanya imbaraga ze neza; utabisobanukiwe azikoresha ku ijana ku ijana cumi rigaragara.', 12, 1);
  insert into public.lessons (module_id, number, title, title_rw, kind, body, body_rw, duration_minutes, sort_order)
  values (m_EP_V1_1, '2', 'History and Evolution of Executive Protection', 'Amateka n''Iterambere ryo Kurinda Abakomeye', 'text', 'Protective work is ancient in principle — rulers have always been guarded — but modern executive protection emerged from a specific sequence of developments. State protective services professionalised first, building doctrine around advance work, motorcade procedure and protective intelligence after a series of assassinations demonstrated that reactive physical presence was insufficient. The commercial sector followed, driven initially by the kidnapping of executives and later by a broader recognition that senior business figures, high-net-worth individuals and public personalities carry risk profiles requiring specialist management.

The most significant evolution in the discipline is the shift from a physical model to an intelligence-led one. The older model positioned officers close to the principal and waited. The current model works to identify a threat during its preparation, using threat assessment methodology, surveillance detection and behavioural indicators, on the reasoning that once an attacker is within contact distance, every remaining option is poor. A second major shift is the growth of low-profile protection: the recognition that visible security can itself attract attention and that blending is frequently more protective than deterring.', 'Umurimo wo kurinda ni uwa kera mu mahame — abategetsi bahoraga barindwa — ariko kurinda abakomeye kw''iki gihe kwavuye mu rutonde rwihariye rw''impinduka. Serivisi z''umutekano za Leta ni zo zabanje kuba umwuga, zubaka inyigisho ku murimo ubanziriza, uburyo bwa konvwa n''amakuru yo kurinda nyuma y''urukurikirane rw''iyicwa ry''abategetsi rwagaragaje ko kugaragara ku mubiri gusa bidahagije. Urwego rw''ubucuruzi rwakurikiye, rutewe mbere na mbere n''ugushimutwa kw''abayobozi hanyuma nyuma no kumenya kwagutse ko abantu bakomeye mu bucuruzi, abafite ubutunzi bwinshi n''abantu bazwi bafite imiterere y''ibyago isaba imicungire y''inzobere.

Impinduka ikomeye kurusha izindi muri uyu mwuga ni ukuva ku buryo bw''umubiri bujya ku buyobowe n''amakuru. Uburyo bwa kera bwashyiraga abakozi hafi y''uwo barinda bakategereza. Uburyo bw''ubu bukora kugira ngo bumenye iterabwoba mu gihe ritegurwa, hakoreshejwe uburyo bwo gusuzuma iterabwoba, kumenya ugukurikiranwa n''ibimenyetso by''imyitwarire, hashingiwe ku kuri ko igihe uwateye ari mu ntera yo kugerwaho, uburyo bwose busigaye ari bubi. Impinduka ya kabiri ikomeye ni ukwiyongera kwo kurinda mu buryo butagaragara: kumenya ko umutekano ugaragara ubwawo ushobora gukurura ubwitonzi kandi ko kwivanga n''abandi akenshi birinda kurusha gukumira.', 12, 2);
  insert into public.lessons (module_id, number, title, title_rw, kind, body, body_rw, duration_minutes, sort_order)
  values (m_EP_V1_1, '3', 'The Role and Responsibilities of an EP Specialist', 'Umurimo n''Inshingano z''Umunyamwuga wa EP', 'text', 'An EP specialist is accountable for a defined set of functions rather than for a general impression of vigilance. Those functions are: contributing to and understanding the threat assessment for the principal; conducting or acting on advance work for every location and route; maintaining continuous situational awareness while on duty; holding an assigned arc of responsibility within a formation and watching it rather than watching the principal; executing movement procedures for foot and vehicle phases; taking correct immediate action if an incident occurs, which is to move the principal away rather than to engage; providing first aid within the limits of training; maintaining absolute confidentiality; and documenting what is required accurately.

Equally important is what the role is not. An EP specialist is not a driver unless assigned as one, not an investigator, not a personal assistant, and not a companion — although the role frequently drifts toward the last of these, and an officer who becomes socially embedded with a principal loses the professional distance that the work requires. The specialist is also not the decision-maker on the principal''s schedule; the specialist advises on risk, and the principal decides.', 'Umunyamwuga wa EP abazwa imirimo yagenwe aho kubazwa ishusho rusange yo kuba maso. Iyo mirimo ni: kugira uruhare no gusobanukirwa isuzuma ry''iterabwoba ku wo barinda; gukora cyangwa gukurikiza umurimo ubanziriza ku hantu no ku nzira byose; kugumana kumenya ibikikuye buhoraho igihe uri ku kazi; kugira igice cy''inshingano yahawe mu miterere y''itsinda no kukireba aho kureba uwo barinda; gushyira mu bikorwa uburyo bwo kugenda ku bice byo ku maguru n''ibyo mu modoka; gufata igikorwa cyihuse gikwiye niba ikibazo kibaye, ari ugukura uwo barinda aho kuhangana; gutanga ubufasha bwa mbere mu mipaka y''amahugurwa; kugumana ibanga ryuzuye; no kwandika ibisabwa neza.

Kimwe n''ingenzi ni icyo uyu murimo utari cyo. Umunyamwuga wa EP si umushoferi keretse yagenwe nk''uwo, si umushakashatsi, si umufasha bwite, kandi si mugenzi — nubwo uyu murimo akenshi wegera icyanyuma muri ibi, kandi umukozi uhinduka inshuti y''uwo barinda atakaza intera y''umwuga uyu murimo usaba. Umunyamwuga kandi si we ufata icyemezo ku gahunda y''uwo barinda; umunyamwuga agira inama ku byago, kandi uwo barinda agafata icyemezo.', 12, 3);
  insert into public.lessons (module_id, number, title, title_rw, kind, body, body_rw, duration_minutes, sort_order)
  values (m_EP_V1_1, '4', 'EP Terminology and Concepts', 'Amagambo n''Imyumvire bya EP', 'text', 'The profession uses a specific vocabulary, and using it precisely matters because ambiguity in a radio transmission or a briefing produces error. Principal: the person being protected. Detail: the team assigned to that person. Advance: the work done at a location before the principal arrives. Working the principal: the officer positioned closest, whose sole function on contact is to move them. Arc of responsibility: the sector each officer observes within a formation. Safe haven: a pre-identified location the principal can be moved to and held securely. Choke point: a place where movement is constrained and options reduce. Attack on principal: any hostile act directed at them. Immediate action: the pre-drilled response — move away, do not engage. Abort criteria: the conditions defined in advance under which a movement is cancelled. Low profile: protection delivered without visible security signature.

Use these terms as defined rather than loosely, and define any term you use that a team member may not share. In a briefing, ambiguity is the same as absence.', 'Uyu mwuga ukoresha amagambo yihariye, kandi kuyakoresha neza bifite akamaro kuko kutumvikana mu butumwa bwa radio cyangwa mu kumenyesha bitanga ikosa. Uwo barinda: umuntu urindwa. Itsinda: itsinda ryagenewe uwo muntu. Umurimo ubanziriza: umurimo ukorwa ku hantu mbere y''uko uwo barinda ageza. Gukorera uwo barinda: umukozi ushyizwe hafi cyane, umurimo we wonyine igihe hari ikibaye ari ukumukura aho. Igice cy''inshingano: agace buri mukozi areba mu miterere y''itsinda. Ahantu h''umutekano: ahantu hamenyekanye mbere uwo barinda ashobora kwimurirwa akabikwa neza. Ahantu hagoye: aho kugenda kugarukiwe n''uburyo bugabanuka. Igitero ku wo barinda: igikorwa cyose cy''urwango kimwerekejeho. Igikorwa cyihuse: igisubizo cyitojwe mbere — kumukura aho, kutahangana. Ibigena guhagarika: imimerere yagenwe mbere urugendo ruhagarikwaho. Kutagaragara: kurinda gutangwa nta kimenyetso cy''umutekano kigaragara.

Koresha aya magambo nk''uko asobanuwe aho kuyakoresha mu buryo budasobanutse, kandi usobanure ijambo iryo ari ryo ryose ukoresha umukozi w''itsinda ashobora kutagira. Mu kumenyesha, kutumvikana ni kimwe no kutabaho.', 12, 4);
