do $$ declare m_EP_V6_2 uuid; a_id uuid; q_id uuid; begin
  if not exists (select 1 from public.courses where id = 'EP-V6') then return; end if;
  insert into public.modules (course_id, number, title, title_rw, intro, intro_rw, sort_order)
  values ('EP-V6', 2, 'Detention, Search, Contracts and Professional Liability', 'Gufunga, Gusaka, Amasezerano n''Inshingano z''Umwuga', 'Subjects 156–162. This module covers arrest and detention limits, search and seizure, contract law, international security law, aviation and maritime provisions, incident reporting obligations and professional liability.', 'Ingingo 156–162. Iki gice kigaruka ku mipaka yo gufata no gufunga, gusaka no gufatira, amategeko y''amasezerano, amategeko mpuzamahanga y''umutekano, ingingo z''indege n''iz''inyanja, inshingano zo gutanga raporo n''inshingano z''umwuga.', 2)
  returning id into m_EP_V6_2;
  insert into public.lessons (module_id, number, title, title_rw, kind, body, body_rw, duration_minutes, sort_order)
  values (m_EP_V6_2, '156', 'Arrest Authority and Its Limitations', 'Ububasha bwo Gufata n''Imipaka Yabwo', 'text', 'In most jurisdictions a private person holds some power of arrest, but it is narrower than commonly believed, is subject to conditions that are easy to fail, and carries substantial consequences when exercised wrongly. The conditions typically include a requirement that an offence of a specified seriousness has actually been committed rather than merely suspected, that the arrest is necessary for a defined reason, and that the person is handed to the police without delay. An arrest that fails any condition is unlawful detention and assault, and the officer — not the organisation — is the person who committed it.

For protective work the guidance is straightforward and should be reflected in the rules of engagement: an EP officer''s mandate is the principal, not law enforcement. Detaining a person removes an officer from the detail, converts a protective operation into a legal proceeding, and creates a static situation at a location the principal is still present in. Except in the narrowest circumstances, the correct action is to remove the principal, record a description and the circumstances, and report to the police, who hold both the authority and the training that the officer does not.', 'Mu bihugu byinshi umuntu ku giti cye afite ububasha bumwe bwo gufata, ariko ni bugufi kurusha uko biyumvishwa, bufite ibisabwa byoroshye kunanirwa, kandi bufite ingaruka nini iyo bukoreshejwe nabi. Ibisabwa akenshi birimo gusaba ko icyaha cy''uburemere bwagenwe cyakozwe koko aho kuba gikekwa gusa, ko gufata ari ngombwa ku mpamvu yagenwe, kandi ko uwo muntu ahererekanywa kuri polisi nta gutinda. Gufata kunaniwe kuzuza igisabwa icyo ari cyo cyose ni ugufunga kutemewe no gukubita, kandi umukozi — atari ikigo — ni we muntu wabikoze.

Ku murimo wo kurinda amabwiriza ni asobanutse kandi agomba kugaragara mu mabwiriza y''ibikorwa: inshingano y''umukozi wa EP ni uwo barinda, atari gukurikirana ibyaha. Gufunga umuntu bikura umukozi ku itsinda, bihindura ibikorwa byo kurinda urubanza, kandi bikora imimerere ihoraho ku hantu uwo barinda akiri. Uretse mu bihe bike cyane, igikorwa gikwiye ni ugukura uwo barinda, kwandika uko uwo muntu asa n''imimerere, no kubimenyesha polisi.', 12, 1);
  insert into public.lessons (module_id, number, title, title_rw, kind, body, body_rw, duration_minutes, sort_order)
  values (m_EP_V6_2, '157', 'Search and Seizure Principles', 'Amahame yo Gusaka no Gufatira', 'text', 'An EP officer has no power to search a person or their property. Where searching occurs lawfully in this field it is by consent, and consent is only meaningful where it is genuinely voluntary and the person understands they may refuse — a search conducted because a person believed they had no choice is not consented to. The common lawful arrangement is conditional entry: a person may be told that entry to private premises or an event requires submitting to a search, and may then choose to submit or to leave. That is lawful because the person retains a real alternative; removing the alternative removes the consent.

Where a search is conducted: explain what will happen and why before beginning; conduct it in a manner and by a person appropriate to the individual, including on gender where relevant; do not go beyond what the stated purpose requires; and record what was done. Seizing property is a separate matter with a higher threshold — an officer who takes a person''s belongings without lawful basis has committed theft, and the fact that the item was prohibited at that venue does not by itself provide one.', 'Umukozi wa EP nta bubasha afite bwo gusaka umuntu cyangwa umutungo we. Aho gusaka bibera mu buryo bwemewe muri uru rwego ni ku bwemere, kandi ubwemere bufite akamaro gusa aho ari ubw''ubushake nyabwo kandi umuntu asobanukiwe ko ashobora kwanga — gusaka byakozwe kuko umuntu yizeraga ko nta bundi buryo afite ntabwo byemerewe. Uburyo busanzwe bwemewe ni ukwinjira kugengwa n''ibisabwa: umuntu ashobora kubwirwa ko kwinjira mu nyubako bwite cyangwa mu birori bisaba kwemera gusakwa, hanyuma agahitamo kwemera cyangwa kugenda. Ibyo byemewe kuko uwo muntu agumana ubundi buryo nyabwo; gukuraho ubwo buryo bikuraho ubwemere.

Aho gusaka bikozwe: sobanura ibizabaho n''impamvu mbere yo gutangira; bikore mu buryo no n''umuntu bikwiye uwo muntu, harimo ku gitsina aho bikenewe; ntukarenge ibyo intego yavuzwe isaba; kandi wandike ibyakozwe. Gufatira ibintu ni ikindi kibazo gifite urwego rwo hejuru — umukozi ufata ibintu by''umuntu nta shingiro ryemewe aba yakoze ubujura.', 12, 2);
  insert into public.lessons (module_id, number, title, title_rw, kind, body, body_rw, duration_minutes, sort_order)
  values (m_EP_V6_2, '158', 'Contract Law Basics', 'Ishingiro ry''Amategeko y''Amasezerano', 'text', 'Many protective professionals work independently or through small companies, which makes contractual competence part of professional competence rather than an administrative afterthought. A protective services contract should state: the scope of the service, described specifically enough that both parties would agree afterwards on what was included; the number of officers, the hours and the locations; what is expressly excluded, which prevents most subsequent disputes; the rate, the payment terms and what happens on late payment; liability allocation and the insurance each party holds; confidentiality obligations and their duration, which survive the engagement; the notice period and termination provisions; and the applicable law and jurisdiction, which matters greatly on international work.

The provisions most often omitted and most often needed are the scope exclusions and the liability allocation. A contract that describes what will be provided without describing what will not invites a client to expect a standard of service that was never priced, and a contract silent on liability allocates it by default in ways neither party intended.', 'Abanyamwuga benshi bo kurinda bakora bigenga cyangwa binyuze mu bigo bito, bigatuma ubushobozi mu masezerano ari igice cy''ubushobozi bw''umwuga aho kuba ikintu cy''imicungire cyo nyuma. Amasezerano ya serivisi zo kurinda agomba kuvuga: ibyo serivisi ikubiyemo, bisobanuwe neza bihagije ku buryo impande zombi zakwemeranya nyuma ku byari birimo; umubare w''abakozi, amasaha n''ahantu; ibitarimo mu buryo bugaragara, bikumira amakimbirane menshi akurikiraho; igiciro, ibisabwa mu kwishyura n''ibibaho ku bwishyu bwatinze; kugabana inshingano n''ubwishingizi buri ruhande rufite; inshingano z''ibanga n''igihe zimara, zikomeza nyuma y''akazi; igihe cyo kumenyesha n''ingingo zo gusesa; n''amategeko akoreshwa n''aho urubanza ruberera, bifite akamaro kanini ku kazi mpuzamahanga.

Ingingo zikunze gusigwa kandi zikunze gukenerwa ni ibitarimo mu byo serivisi ikubiyemo no kugabana inshingano. Amasezerano asobanura ibizatangwa atasobanura ibitazatangwa atumira umukiriya kwitega urwego rwa serivisi rutigeze rugenerwa igiciro.', 12, 3);
  insert into public.lessons (module_id, number, title, title_rw, kind, body, body_rw, duration_minutes, sort_order)
  values (m_EP_V6_2, '159', 'International Security Law', 'Amategeko Mpuzamahanga y''Umutekano', 'text', 'Working across borders raises legal questions domestic work does not, and the most consequential of them must be answered before travel rather than discovered on arrival. Establish: whether protective work is lawful in that country at all and whether it requires licensing; whether a foreign detail may operate or whether local partnership is mandatory; the law on equipment, since items entirely lawful at home are prohibited on arrival in many jurisdictions and possession may be a serious offence; the law on detention, search, self-defence and use of force, which varies substantially and cannot be assumed; visa and work authorisation requirements, since operating on a tourist visa may itself be an offence; and the position on carrying protective equipment across borders.

Beyond national law, international humanitarian and human rights frameworks constrain conduct particularly where armed actors are present, and industry standards for private security providers in complex environments set expectations on vetting, training, use of force and accountability that clients increasingly require. Establish which apply, and never assume that a practice lawful in one jurisdiction transfers to another.', 'Gukorera hakurya y''imipaka bizana ibibazo by''amategeko umurimo wo mu gihugu utazana, kandi ibifite ingaruka kurusha ibindi bigomba gusubizwa mbere y''urugendo aho kubimenya ugeze. Menya: niba umurimo wo kurinda wemewe muri icyo gihugu na gato n''ukuba usaba impushya; niba itsinda ry''abanyamahanga ryemerewe gukora cyangwa ukuba ubufatanye bwo mu karere ari itegeko; amategeko ku bikoresho, kuko ibintu byemewe burundu iwanyu bibujijwe ugeze mu bihugu byinshi kandi kubifite bishobora kuba icyaha gikomeye; amategeko ku gufunga, gusaka, kwirwanaho no gukoresha imbaraga, atandukanye cyane kandi adashobora kwiyumvishwa; ibisabwa kuri viza n''uruhushya rwo gukora, kuko gukorera kuri viza y''ubukerarugendo bishobora kuba icyaha ubwabyo; n''umwanya ku gutwara ibikoresho byo kurinda hakurya y''imipaka.

Hejuru y''amategeko y''igihugu, inzego mpuzamahanga z''ikiremwamuntu n''iz''uburenganzira bwa muntu zigarukira imyitwarire cyane cyane aho hari abitwaje intwaro.', 12, 4);
  insert into public.lessons (module_id, number, title, title_rw, kind, body, body_rw, duration_minutes, sort_order)
  values (m_EP_V6_2, '160', 'Aviation and Maritime Security Law', 'Amategeko y''Umutekano w''Indege n''Inyanja', 'text', 'Aviation and maritime environments operate under their own legal regimes, and in both the detail''s authority is displaced by that of the operator. On an aircraft the captain holds authority over everyone aboard, including a protective detail, and their instruction is binding — an officer who acts contrary to it commits an offence in most jurisdictions. Items entirely ordinary in protective work are prohibited in cabin baggage and frequently in hold baggage, and declaration requirements apply. Behaviour that would be unremarkable elsewhere may constitute an aviation offence, and the threshold is low.

At sea the master holds equivalent authority, jurisdiction depends on the vessel''s flag and its position relative to territorial waters, and the applicable law may change during a voyage without anything visible changing. In both environments the practical guidance is the same: establish the position before travelling rather than at the point of embarkation, declare what must be declared, comply with the operator''s instructions, and understand that the detail''s own procedures are subordinate to the regime governing that environment.', 'Ahantu h''indege n''ah''inyanja bikorera mu nzego zabyo z''amategeko, kandi muri byombi ububasha bw''itsinda busimburwa n''ubw''ukoresha. Mu ndege kapiteni afite ububasha ku bantu bose bari mu ndege, harimo n''itsinda ririnda, kandi itegeko rye ni ngombwa — umukozi ukora binyuranye na ryo akora icyaha mu bihugu byinshi. Ibintu bisanzwe burundu mu murimo wo kurinda bibujijwe mu mizigo yinjizwa mu ndege kandi akenshi no mu ibitse, kandi ibisabwa byo gutangaza birakoreshwa. Imyitwarire itari kugaragara ahandi ishobora kuba icyaha cy''indege, kandi urwego ruri hasi.

Mu nyanja umuyobozi w''ubwato afite ububasha bumwe, ububasha bw''urukiko bushingira ku ibendera ry''ubwato n''aho buri ugereranyije n''amazi y''igihugu, kandi amategeko akoreshwa ashobora guhinduka mu rugendo nta kintu kigaragara gihindutse. Mu hantu hombi amabwiriza afatika ni amwe: menya umwanya mbere y''urugendo aho kuwumenya wurira, tangaza ibigomba gutangazwa, kubahiriza amabwiriza y''ukoresha.', 12, 5);
  insert into public.lessons (module_id, number, title, title_rw, kind, body, body_rw, duration_minutes, sort_order)
  values (m_EP_V6_2, '161', 'Reporting Legal Incidents', 'Gutanga Raporo ku Bibazo by''Amategeko', 'text', 'Certain incidents carry a legal obligation to report, and the obligation is frequently time-bound and short. The categories typically include: any use of force; any injury however apparently minor; any detention or restraint; a road traffic collision; a data breach; a weapons-related incident where applicable; a death; and any allegation of misconduct against an officer. The organisation should hold a written schedule stating what must be reported, to whom, within what period and by what means, because an officer under pressure will not construct that analysis independently.

Report promptly and factually, recording observed fact with exact times and precise locations and distinguishing clearly between what was observed, what was reported by others and what was inferred. Never delay a report to establish the outcome or to consult about how it will be received: late reporting is treated as concealment, and a report that arrives after the regulator, the client or the family has learned of the incident from another source has damaged the organisation''s position more than the incident itself did.', 'Ibibazo bimwe bifite inshingano y''amategeko yo gutangwaho raporo, kandi iyo nshingano akenshi ifite igihe ntarengwa kandi gito. Ibyiciro akenshi birimo: gukoresha imbaraga kose; ikomere iryo ari ryo ryose uko ryagaragara nk''irito kose; gufunga cyangwa kubuza umuntu kose; impanuka y''imodoka; ivuka ry''amakuru; ikibazo kijyanye n''intwaro aho bikoreshwa; urupfu; n''ikirego icyo ari cyo cyose cy''imyitwarire mibi ku mukozi. Ikigo kigomba kugira gahunda yanditse ivuga ibigomba gutangwaho raporo, kuri nde, mu gihe kingana iki no mu buryo ki, kuko umukozi uri mu gitutu atazakora iryo sesengura ubwe.

Tanga raporo vuba kandi ushingiye ku byabaye, wandika ibyabonetse n''amasaha nyayo n''ahantu nyaho kandi utandukanya neza ibyabonetse, ibyatanzwe n''abandi n''ibyiyumvishijwe. Ntukigere utinza raporo kugira ngo umenye icyavuyemo cyangwa ngo ubaze uko izakirwa: gutanga raporo bitinze bifatwa nk''ukuhisha.', 12, 6);
  insert into public.lessons (module_id, number, title, title_rw, kind, body, body_rw, duration_minutes, sort_order)
  values (m_EP_V6_2, '162', 'Professional Liability', 'Inshingano z''Umwuga', 'text', 'Professional liability is the exposure an officer or organisation carries for the quality of the work itself, as distinct from liability for a specific act. It arises where the service delivered fell below the standard a competent professional would have provided: an assessment that missed what a competent assessor would have found, advice that was wrong, a plan that was inadequate, an officer deployed without the qualification the role required, or a control recommended and then never verified.

Three things reduce it materially. Insurance: hold appropriate professional indemnity and public liability cover and confirm that it extends to the countries and activities involved, because a policy that excludes the work you are doing is not cover. Competence honesty: never accept an assignment beyond your capability, since doing so transfers the risk to the principal and is indefensible afterwards regardless of how it turns out. And documentation: a defensible record of what was assessed, what was recommended, what the client accepted and what they declined is the single strongest protection available, and its absence is why organisations that acted reasonably frequently cannot demonstrate that they did.', 'Inshingano z''umwuga ni ibyago umukozi cyangwa ikigo gifite ku bwiza bw''umurimo ubwawo, bitandukanye n''inshingano ku gikorwa runaka. Zivuka aho serivisi yatanzwe yari munsi y''urwego umunyamwuga ufite ubushobozi yari gutanga: isuzuma ryabuze ibyo umusuzumyi ufite ubushobozi yari kubona, inama itari yo, gahunda idahagije, umukozi washyizwe ku murimo adafite icyemezo umurimo wasabaga, cyangwa igenzura ryatanzwe hanyuma ntiryigere ryemezwa.

Ibintu bitatu bizigabanya cyane. Ubwishingizi: gira ubwishingizi bukwiye bw''umwuga n''ubw''inshingano ku baturage kandi wemeze ko bugera ku bihugu n''ibikorwa bireba, kuko politiki isiga umurimo urimo gukora atari ubwishingizi. Ubunyakuri ku bushobozi: ntukigere wemera akazi karenze ubushobozi bwawe, kuko kubikora bwohereza ibyago ku wo barinda kandi bidashobora kwiregurwa nyuma uko byagenda kose. N''inyandiko: inyandiko ishobora kwiregurwa y''ibyasuzumwe, ibyatanzwe nk''icyifuzo, ibyo umukiriya yemeye n''ibyo yanze ni bwo burinzi bukomeye kurusha ubundi buhari.', 12, 7);
  insert into public.assessments (course_id, module_id, title, title_rw, kind, pass_mark, sort_order)
  values ('EP-V6', m_EP_V6_2, 'Quiz — Detention, Search, Contracts and Professional Liability', 'Ikizamini — Gufunga, Gusaka, Amasezerano n''Inshingano z''Umwuga', 'quiz', 70, 2)
