do $$ declare m_EP_V8_2 uuid; a_id uuid; q_id uuid; begin
  if not exists (select 1 from public.courses where id = 'EP-V8') then return; end if;
  insert into public.modules (course_id, number, title, title_rw, intro, intro_rw, sort_order)
  values ('EP-V8', 2, 'Team Development, Discipline and Command', 'Iterambere ry''Itsinda, Umurava n''Ubuyobozi', 'Subjects 184–189. This module covers team motivation, conflict resolution, professional discipline, operational command, mission briefing leadership and risk-based decision-making.', 'Ingingo 184–189. Iki gice kigaruka ku gushishikariza itsinda, gucyuha amakimbirane, umurava w''umwuga, ubuyobozi bw''ibikorwa, ubuyobozi mu kumenyesha ubutumwa no gufata ibyemezo bishingiye ku byago.', 2)
  returning id into m_EP_V8_2;
  insert into public.lessons (module_id, number, title, title_rw, kind, body, body_rw, duration_minutes, sort_order)
  values (m_EP_V8_2, '184', 'Team Motivation', 'Gushishikariza Itsinda', 'text', 'Motivation in protective work faces a structural difficulty that most other roles do not: the product is an absence. A well-run assignment produces a day on which nothing happened, and an officer who does the work perfectly for six months has nothing visible to show for it. That is why motivation in this field cannot rest on outcome and must rest on something else.

What works is being taken seriously. An officer whose incident report visibly leads to a change, whose observation is acted on, whose shift is properly relieved, who is briefed rather than merely instructed, and whose development is invested in performs measurably better and stays considerably longer than one treated as interchangeable. What does not work is exhortation, and what actively damages motivation is the discovery that standards apply to junior officers and not to senior ones. Recognise the invisible work explicitly — the advance nobody saw, the check that found nothing, the report on a quiet night — because if only incidents are noticed, the team learns that only incidents matter, and an operation that has learned that is one incident away from discovering otherwise.', 'Gushishikariza mu murimo wo kurinda bihura n''ingorane y''imiterere indi mirimo myinshi itahura na yo: igicuruzwa ni ukutabaho. Akazi kacunzwe neza gatanga umunsi nta cyabaye, kandi umukozi ukora umurimo neza mu mezi atandatu nta kintu kigaragara afite cyo kwerekana. Ni yo mpamvu gushishikariza muri uru rwego bidashobora gushingira ku cyavuyemo kandi bigomba gushingira ku kindi.

Ibikora ni ugufatwa uko ukwiye. Umukozi raporo ye y''ikibazo igaragara ko yatumye habaho impinduka, icyo yabonye gikorerwaho, usimburwa neza ku kazi, umenyeshwa aho gutegekwa gusa, kandi ushorwamo mu iterambere akora neza bigaragara kandi aguma igihe kirekire cyane kurusha ufatwa nk''usimburana n''undi. Ibitakora ni ugushishikariza mu magambo, kandi ikintu cyangiza gushishikariza ni ukumenya ko urwego rukurikizwa ku bakozi bato rutakurikizwa ku bakuru. Menya umurimo utagaragara mu buryo bugaragara — umurimo ubanziriza nta muntu wabonye, igenzura ritabonye ikintu, raporo yo mu ijoro rituje.', 12, 1);
  insert into public.lessons (module_id, number, title, title_rw, kind, body, body_rw, duration_minutes, sort_order)
  values (m_EP_V8_2, '185', 'Conflict Resolution', 'Gucyuha Amakimbirane', 'text', 'Conflict within a protective detail is common because the work attracts confident, experienced people with strong views about correct practice, and it is not in itself a problem — a technical disagreement resolved through evidence improves the operation. It becomes damaging when it goes unaddressed, when it becomes personal rather than technical, or when it is conducted in front of the principal or the client, which destroys the authority of everyone involved including the person who was right.

The method is to address it early and directly, in private, separating the technical question from the interpersonal one and dealing with each in its own terms. Decide the technical point on evidence and document the decision so it does not recur. Where the issue is conduct rather than opinion, treat it as a performance matter and handle it promptly, because a conduct problem left unaddressed in a small team is known to everyone within a week and sets the operating standard more effectively than any policy statement. And never allow a conflict to be resolved by seniority alone where evidence is available, since a team that learns decisions follow rank rather than reasoning stops offering reasoning.', 'Amakimbirane mu itsinda ririnda ni asanzwe kuko umurimo ukurura abantu bafite icyizere, inararibonye, bafite ibitekerezo bikomeye ku byo gukora neza, kandi ubwayo si ikibazo — ukudahuza ku buhanga gukemuwe hakoreshejwe ibimenyetso kunoza ibikorwa. Aba akaga iyo atacyuwe, iyo ahindutse ay''umuntu ku giti cye aho kuba ay''ubuhanga, cyangwa iyo akorewe imbere y''uwo barinda cyangwa umukiriya, bisenya ubutware bwa buri wese wabigizemo uruhare harimo n''uwari afite ukuri.

Uburyo ni ukuyacyuha kare kandi mu buryo butaziguye, mu bwiherero, utandukanya ikibazo cy''ubuhanga n''icy''imibanire ukacyuha buri kimwe mu buryo bwacyo. Fata icyemezo ku ngingo y''ubuhanga ushingiye ku bimenyetso kandi wandike icyo cyemezo kugira ngo kitazongera. Aho ikibazo ari imyitwarire aho kuba igitekerezo, kifate nk''ikibazo cy''imikorere ukicyuhe vuba, kuko ikibazo cy''imyitwarire kitacyuwe mu itsinda rito kimenywa na buri wese mu cyumweru kandi kigashyiraho urwego rw''akazi kurusha ivuga rya politiki iryo ari ryo ryose.', 12, 2);
  insert into public.lessons (module_id, number, title, title_rw, kind, body, body_rw, duration_minutes, sort_order)
  values (m_EP_V8_2, '186', 'Professional Discipline', 'Umurava w''Umwuga', 'text', 'Professional discipline in this field is the practice of maintaining a standard when nothing depends on it visibly and nobody is watching, which describes the overwhelming majority of protective work. It is the officer who checks the radio at the start of a shift on which they are confident nothing will happen, who conducts the advance properly when the schedule is running late, who writes the occurrence log on a quiet night, and who challenges a person who appears to belong.

Discipline is established by leadership behaviour rather than by policy. A team lead who skips an advance because time was short has established that the advance is optional, whatever the manual says. A supervisor who waives a standard once for a senior officer has established that the standard is negotiable. Conversely, a lead who visibly declines a venue on safety grounds and accepts the commercial awkwardness that follows has established something more durable than any written standard could. Handle lapses proportionately and promptly, distinguishing an error from a pattern and a mistake from a failure of integrity — a concealed error is a different category from the error itself.', 'Umurava w''umwuga muri uru rwego ni imikorere yo kugumisha urwego igihe nta kintu gishingiye kuri rwo bigaragara kandi nta muntu ureba, bisobanura igice kinini cyane cy''umurimo wo kurinda. Ni umukozi ugenzura radio mu ntangiriro y''akazi yizeye ko nta cyo kizabaho, ukora umurimo ubanziriza neza igihe gahunda itinze, wandika igitabo cy''ibibaye mu ijoro rituje, kandi ubaza umuntu ugaragara nk''uwaho.

Umurava ushyirwaho n''imyitwarire y''ubuyobozi aho gushyirwaho na politiki. Umuyobozi w''itsinda usimbuka umurimo ubanziriza kuko igihe cyari gito aba yashyizeho ko umurimo ubanziriza ari uw''ihitamo, uko igitabo kivuga kose. Umugenzuzi urengagiza urwego rimwe ku mukozi mukuru aba yashyizeho ko urwego ruvugwaho. Ubundi, umuyobozi wanga ahantu ku mpamvu z''umutekano bigaragara akemera ingorane y''ubucuruzi ikurikiraho aba yashyizeho ikintu kirambye kurusha urwego rwanditse rwose rwashobora. Cyuha amakosa mu buryo buhuye kandi vuba, utandukanya ikosa n''uburyo busubirwamo n''ikosa n''ukunanirwa kw''ubudahemuka.', 12, 3);
  insert into public.lessons (module_id, number, title, title_rw, kind, body, body_rw, duration_minutes, sort_order)
  values (m_EP_V8_2, '187', 'Operational Command', 'Ubuyobozi bw''Ibikorwa', 'text', 'Operational command is the exercise of authority during an engagement, and it rests on one thing being unambiguous: every officer must be able to state who commands and who deputises without being asked twice. Ambiguity about who decides is the most common cause of delayed response in this field, because officers unsure of the chain wait for permission nobody is issuing, and the seconds spent waiting are frequently the only seconds that existed.

Command is exercised differently by phase. During planning and review, a participative style produces better results, because officers on the ground see what the commander does not. During the engagement, and particularly during an incident, the style is directive: instructions are given and followed without debate, because there is no time to build consensus while a situation is developing. Command also transfers, and the transfer points must be defined in advance: to the deputy if the commander is unavailable or is themselves involved in the incident, and to an emergency service where a major incident is declared — after which the detail supports rather than continuing to direct, with the single exception that responsibility for the principal''s immediate protection remains with the detail throughout.', 'Ubuyobozi bw''ibikorwa ni ugukoresha ububasha mu gihe cy''akazi, kandi bushingiye ku kintu kimwe kidashidikanywaho: buri mukozi agomba gushobora kuvuga uyobora n''umusimbura atabajijwe kabiri. Kutamenya ufata icyemezo ni yo mpamvu ikunze gutera gutinda kw''igisubizo muri uru rwego, kuko abakozi batazi urutonde bategereza uruhushya nta muntu urutanga.

Ubuyobozi bukoreshwa mu buryo butandukanye ku cyiciro. Mu gutegura no gusuzuma, uburyo bw''ubufatanye butanga ibyavuyemo byiza, kuko abakozi bari ku murima babona ibyo umuyobozi atabona. Mu gihe cy''akazi, cyane cyane mu gihe cy''ikibazo, uburyo ni ubutegeka: amabwiriza atangwa akubahirizwa nta mpaka, kuko nta gihe cyo kubaka ubwumvikane mu gihe ibintu bigenda bikura. Ubuyobozi kandi burimurwa, kandi ahantu bwimurirwa hagomba kugenwa mbere: ku musimbura niba umuyobozi adahari cyangwa ubwe abigizemo uruhare, no ku rwego rw''abatabazi aho ikibazo gikomeye cyatangajwe — nyuma yaho itsinda rishyigikira aho gukomeza kuyobora.', 12, 4);
  insert into public.lessons (module_id, number, title, title_rw, kind, body, body_rw, duration_minutes, sort_order)
  values (m_EP_V8_2, '188', 'Mission Briefing Leadership', 'Ubuyobozi mu Kumenyesha Ubutumwa', 'text', 'The briefing is where a plan becomes a shared understanding, and a team that has been given a document but not briefed has not been briefed. Deliver the same structure every time so that nothing is omitted when time is short, and lead it personally rather than delegating it, because the briefing is also where the commander demonstrates that the plan is understood, that the standard is expected and that questions are welcome.

Confirm understanding by asking individual officers to state their own post and their first action in an emergency, rather than asking whether everyone understood — the second question produces agreement, which is worthless, and it also removes the officer''s opportunity to admit uncertainty. Invite questions genuinely: a commander who signals impatience receives none, and the questions not asked are the gaps that appear later. Brief non-detail personnel who hold a role — a driver, a venue liaison, a household member — because a person with a task who does not know the stop signal is a gap in the plan. And end with the abort criteria, so the last thing the team hears is the circumstance in which they stop.', 'Kumenyesha ni ho gahunda ihindukira gusobanukirwa gusangiwe, kandi itsinda ryahawe inyandiko ritamenyeshejwe ntiryamenyeshejwe. Tanga imiterere imwe buri gihe kugira ngo nta kirengagizwa igihe gito, kandi ubiyobore ubwawe aho kubihereza undi, kuko kumenyesha ari na ho umuyobozi agaragaza ko gahunda yumvikanye, ko urwego rutegerejwe kandi ko ibibazo byakirwa.

Emeza gusobanukirwa usaba abakozi buri wese kuvuga umurimo we n''igikorwa cye cya mbere mu byihutirwa, aho kubaza niba bose basobanukiwe — ikibazo cya kabiri gitanga kwemera, nta gaciro gifite, kandi kikanakuraho amahirwe y''umukozi yo kwemera ko ashidikanya. Tumira ibibazo mu bunyakuri: umuyobozi ugaragaza ko yihuta ntawe abibaza, kandi ibibazo bitabajijwe ni byo byuho bigaragara nyuma. Menyesha abatari mu itsinda bafite umurimo — umushoferi, uhagarariye ahantu, umuntu wo mu rugo — kuko umuntu ufite umurimo utazi ikimenyetso cyo guhagarara ari icyuho muri gahunda. Kandi usoze n''ibipimo byo guhagarika.', 12, 5);
  insert into public.lessons (module_id, number, title, title_rw, kind, body, body_rw, duration_minutes, sort_order)
  values (m_EP_V8_2, '189', 'Risk-Based Decision-Making', 'Gufata Ibyemezo Bishingiye ku Byago', 'text', 'A protective leader''s decisions are almost always trade-offs rather than choices between a right and a wrong option: a route that is more secure but longer, a measure that reduces exposure but constrains the principal, an assignment that is commercially valuable but stretches capability. Risk-based decision-making is the discipline of making those trade-offs explicit rather than resolving them by instinct.

The method is: state what the decision is actually about; identify what each option exposes and what it protects; assess likelihood and consequence for each rather than reasoning from the worst case, since a leader who always plans for the worst case will recommend measures no client will accept and no principal will tolerate; state what you are accepting under each option and be explicit that you are accepting it; make the decision at the level it belongs, since a decision that should be the client''s — accepting a residual risk, funding a control, declining a venue — is not the detail leader''s to make silently; and record the reasoning, because a decision taken with incomplete information will be examined afterwards with hindsight, and the record of why is what distinguishes a judgement from a mistake.', 'Ibyemezo by''umuyobozi wo kurinda hafi buri gihe ni ibyo guhitamo hagati y''ibintu bifite ibyiza n''ibibi aho kuba guhitamo hagati y''icyiza n''ikibi: inzira ifite umutekano ariko ndende, ingamba igabanya kugaragara ariko igarukira uwo barinda, akazi gafite agaciro mu bucuruzi ariko kagura ubushobozi. Gufata ibyemezo bishingiye ku byago ni umurava wo gutuma ibyo guhitamo bigaragara aho kubikemura n''imyumvire.

Uburyo ni: kuvuga icyo icyemezo kireba koko; kumenya icyo buri buryo bugaragaza n''icyo burinda; gusuzuma amahirwe n''ingaruka kuri buri bumwe aho gutekereza uhereye ku bibi kurusha ibindi, kuko umuyobozi uhora ateganya ibibi kurusha ibindi azatanga ingamba nta mukiriya uzemera kandi nta wo barinda uzihanganira; kuvuga icyo wemera kuri buri buryo kandi ukavuga neza ko urikwemera; gufata icyemezo ku rwego rukigenewe, kuko icyemezo kigomba kuba icy''umukiriya — kwemera ikibazo gisigaye, gutanga amafaranga ku genzura, kwanga ahantu — kitari icy''umuyobozi w''itsinda gufata mu bwiherero; no kwandika impamvu.', 12, 6);
  insert into public.assessments (course_id, module_id, title, title_rw, kind, pass_mark, sort_order)
